## Summary

**Goal:** audit Helios When's invitation system before a whole-school invitation to the Friday movie night, "Outdoor Movie Night: Dogman" (an HCA-Team activity, /g/movie, Nov 6 2026). Production was read only: no production writes, no mail, and timing work ran on a local production snapshot. Done by opus and gpt-6.1-sol as a pair. Opus took audience, permissions, RSVP and UI; sol took delivery, recipients and calendar. Each independently verified the other's fixes.

**Fixed:**
- **RSVPs counted as sign-ups.** Answering an activity's invitation mailed Team Notices "New sign-up: X for … Going"; this was already happening in production. `MembershipMailer.mail` now skips groups that serve another group (`m.serves`).
- **Double sends.** The invitation write path (`writeGuests` in invitations.go) now refuses inside the transaction anyone who already has a copy (409) or is named twice in one request (400). It covers invite, add-guests, the outside-guest calls and auto-invite. The Pending window disables Send while it runs and closes and refreshes on a refusal.
- **Bulk delivery.** The mailer saves sent-stamps every 50 copies with a flush, where it used to save once at the end of the pass. It rereads the event before each copy, so a closed or cancelled event stops its queued invitations.
- **Parent duplicates.** A student's copy leaves off parents who have their own copy of the same message. Before, a whole-school send gave 240 parents 2 copies and 59 parents 3.
- **Calendar identity.** Calendar files keep the original invitation's organizer and guest link.
- **Declined-RSVP privacy.** Enforced in policy (`declines`, `runs_answers`), so existing data needs no migration. Non-hosts see decliners as "Invited", and My RSVP keeps the household's real answer.

**Key decisions:**
- Saving delivery progress per copy was rejected: about 1,080 Sheets writes, against a quota of about 60 a minute, and `logging.Fatal` on a refused write. Batches of 50 are the trade, at the cost of possibly resending up to 50 after a crash.
- Privacy went in policy rather than a data migration. Measured +3.7% on a parent's heaviest read; shipped queries within noise.

**Left out:**
- Send latency: 539 recipients take 1.7–2.5s, caused by the store rebuilding after every edit in `stageEdits`. Too risky to change before Friday.
- Guests added to an activity by hand becoming HCA-Team volunteers; filed in TODO.md.

**Setup Ian had to do before sending:** set the activity's Loop list (movie@loop.heliosian.com) posting and replying to managers, so the 540 people on the list can't mail each other; add co-chairs in HCA-Team, since the event had no hosts.

